{"title":"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/d/3ed201be08eedf3a35c18c7aa50006ef8e737e53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be digits with\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/5/245fb2387e465e04164cd72cf11fe858db1a90b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(100A+10M+C)(A+M+C) = 2005.\\]\" width=\"320\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/a/bcae71d6a3ee9a0eae5ed0761cd958a2ad39e225.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\mathrm {A}) \\ 1 \\qquad (\\mathrm {B}) \\ 2 \\qquad (\\mathrm {C})\\ 3 \\qquad (\\mathrm {D}) \\ 4 \\qquad (\\mathrm {E})\\ 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"342\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Clearly the two quantities are both integers, so we check the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prime_factorization\" title=\"Prime factorization\">prime factorization</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/3/26324860cbb539eb05e397ca5563d5c9b5971541.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2005 = 5 \\cdot 401$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"109\" height=\"13\" />. It is easy to see now that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bb475e68d419facf3383b4f7fa9fb2684d1947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A,M,C) = (4,0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" /> works, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/b/bfbf4df7c25681bb178ddc50ee0c0d656aa25b5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A\">2005 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\"